{"id": "tea:sanmati-tarka:1.3", "source": "src:sanmati-tarka", "location": {"ref": "1.3", "chapter": "1", "verse": "3", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "The root expounders of the Tīrthaṅkara's word, in its collective and particular aspects, are the substance-standpoint and the mode-standpoint; the others are their subdivisions.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["sound-language"], "terms": ["trm:dravyarthika", "trm:paryayarthika", "trm:naya"], "concepts": ["cpt:nayavada"], "teachers": ["tch:siddhasena-divakara"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Kāṇḍa 1; gāthā number recalled.", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sanmati-tarka:3.47", "source": "src:sanmati-tarka", "location": {"ref": "3.47", "chapter": "3", "verse": "47", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "As many as are the ways of speaking, so many are the standpoint-doctrines; as many as are the standpoint-doctrines, so many are the other doctrines (parasamaya).", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["sound-language", "dispute"], "terms": ["trm:naya", "trm:para-samaya"], "concepts": ["cpt:nayavada", "cpt:jain-views-of-other-darsanas"], "teachers": ["tch:siddhasena-divakara"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Number recalled (3.47).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sanmati-tarka:3.53", "source": "src:sanmati-tarka", "location": {"ref": "3.53"}, "paraphrase": "Time, own-nature, destiny, former deeds and human effort, each held one-sidedly as the cause, are wrong views; taken together they are right view.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": "dravyarthika", "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "dispute"], "original": {"text": "kālo sahāva niyaī puvvakayaṃ purisakāraṇegaṃtā / micchattaṃ te ceva u samāsao honti sammattaṃ", "script": "IAST", "edition": "as quoted in the Abhidhāna-rājendra (checked locally)", "licence": "ancient text (public domain); e-text consulted read-only for reference"}, "terms": ["trm:niyati", "trm:svabhava", "trm:purisakara", "trm:kala-vada"], "concepts": ["cpt:five-causes-jain", "cpt:niyativada"], "teachers": ["tch:siddhasena-divakara"], "disputes": ["dsp:niyati-or-effort"], "notes": "Verse number 3.53 from memory; wording checked as quoted. The naya tag is a best fit (the verse synthesises one-sided standpoints).", "coverage": ["B1", "B2"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U33-sramana"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U33-sramana"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sanmati-tarka:3.69", "source": "src:sanmati-tarka", "location": {"ref": "3.69", "chapter": "3", "verse": "69", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "Blessed be the Jina's word, which is the aggregate of the wrong views, the essence of nectar, easily reached by those who long for release.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["sound-language", "ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:jain-views-of-other-darsanas", "cpt:anekantavada"], "teachers": ["tch:siddhasena-divakara"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "The closing gāthā of the Sanmati (numbered 69 or 70); wording recalled only in substance.", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sanmati-tarka:kanda-1", "source": "src:sanmati-tarka", "location": {"ref": "kanda-1", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "Each standpoint taken by itself, excluding the others, is false; the standpoints joined together and mutually dependent are right view — like separate gems that become a necklace only when strung together.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["sound-language", "ultimate"], "terms": ["trm:naya", "trm:ekanta"], "concepts": ["cpt:nayavada", "cpt:anekantavada"], "obstacles": ["obs:ekanta-view"], "teachers": ["tch:siddhasena-divakara"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "The necklace simile recalled; exact gāthās not checked.", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sanmati-tarka:kanda-2", "source": "src:sanmati-tarka", "location": {"ref": "kanda-2", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "In the omniscient, knowledge and perception are not two cognitions occurring in succession or at once, but one: when all obstruction is gone, the distinction of general and particular grasping falls away.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "dispute"], "terms": ["trm:kevala-jnana", "trm:kevala-darsana"], "concepts": ["cpt:kevala-jnana"], "teachers": ["tch:siddhasena-divakara"], "disputes": ["dsp:kevala-jnana-darsana-sequence"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
